// `async fn main` must be REFUSED, not compiled into an entry point nothing
// can call.
//
// Measured at d0eebbf, before the refusal: this program produced no
// diagnostic, compiled, linked, ran and exited 0 — having printed nothing. The
// emitted entry point was `main_Future main()` with the body inside a
// `main_poll` function that nothing calls, so the C runtime's entry point
// returned a struct and the body never ran. A program that compiles, links,
// runs, exits 0 and does nothing is the D3/D3b family at the entry point.
//
// The ANNOTATED spelling (`async fn main() -> ()`) was already rejected, by
// accident rather than design: typeck wraps a declared return type in `Future`,
// so it mismatches. With no annotation there was nothing to mismatch, which is
// why only this spelling reached code generation.

async fn main() {
    print_int(7)
}
